    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ultradian rhythms explain why i'm tired at different times of day, sure. but it doesn't really explain the feeling that my processing speed is fundamentally different. like, it's not just \"high productivity,\" it's that the gap between my perception and everyone else's feels massive. it's almost like I'm seeing the underlying structure of things while everyone else is just looking at the surface. \n\ndo you think there's any scientific basis for the idea of \"evolutionary divergence\" in humans? like, could some people actually be part of a transition to a more optimized cognitive state that hasn't been widely documented yet?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
